2b. Poppler encoding data (inside the pdf-docx and pdf-pptx modules)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `soffice.data` of the `pdf-docx` and `pdf-pptx` modules includes four
character-collection tables from poppler-data 0.4.12, the encoding-data
package LibreOffice pins for its PDF import (`download.lst`,
`poppler-data-0.4.12.tar.gz`). They map the glyphs of Chinese, Japanese and
Korean CID fonts to Unicode text:

    share/xpdfimport/poppler_data/cidToUnicode/Adobe-CNS1
    share/xpdfimport/poppler_data/cidToUnicode/Adobe-GB1
    share/xpdfimport/poppler_data/cidToUnicode/Adobe-Japan1
    share/xpdfimport/poppler_data/cidToUnicode/Adobe-Korea1

These files are Copyright Glyph & Cog, LLC, and are licensed under the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or version 3, per poppler-data's own
`COPYING`. They are distributed unmodified, and as part of the modules
conveyed under GPLv3 described in section 2a. The files are plain-text
tables and are their own source.

